WEBVTT

00:00:00.010 --> 00:00:05.242
We will use one example repeatedly so the architecture stays easy to follow.

00:00:05.242 --> 00:00:10.907
The user asks: order one zero four two was delivered twenty days ago.

00:00:10.907 --> 00:00:13.947
Can I still return it and get a refund?

00:00:13.947 --> 00:00:16.602
There are two kinds of information here.

00:00:16.602 --> 00:00:19.042
First, we need policy knowledge.

00:00:19.042 --> 00:00:21.282
What is the normal return window?

00:00:21.282 --> 00:00:28.121
Are there exceptions? That information is likely in unstructured documents and is a good fit for retrieval.

00:00:28.737 --> 00:00:31.399
Second, we need order facts.

00:00:31.399 --> 00:00:34.149
What was the authoritative delivery date?

00:00:34.149 --> 00:00:36.399
What is the order status?

00:00:36.399 --> 00:00:41.684
That information is structured and belongs in a database or A P I lookup.

00:00:41.684 --> 00:00:43.903
The final answer depends on both.

00:00:44.475 --> 00:00:49.397
This is a strong agentic example because one source is not enough.

00:00:49.397 --> 00:00:56.308
It also shows why tool choice should match the type of data rather than using vector search for everything.
